I-Frame changes by Cal M =3

Updated the PlayerStats script to make the player invincible while their sprite is flashing.

In order to use this script, replace the game's existing PlayerStats.cs script with the on in this repo.

In order to configure if / how long the player is invincible, select the player prefab. I reccomend editing the base prefab in the project bin rather than in the scene hierarchy, that way your changes are saved across scenes. 

In the prefab editor, select "player" in the Hierarchy. This is the game object that stores the customizable values. You can also edit player movement settings in here!

Scroll down to "Player Stats", click on the "Others" button. This will show you the i-frame settings. 

Toggling "Flashes On Damage" will enable/disable i-frames as well as the player flashing animations.

"Flash Duration" is how long your i-frames last, in seconds.

"Flash Speed" configures how quickly the animation is. Does not affect how i-frames are applied to the player.